PAGE cover
LAYOUT cover
TITLE Morning Routine Planner

PAGE welcome
LAYOUT prose
TITLE Welcome
SUBTITLE The first hour is the only one you control
BLOCK Why the morning and not the day
TEXT By ten in the morning the day belongs to other people. Meetings arrive, messages arrive, other people's urgency arrives. The hour before that is the only reliably uncontested time most of us get, which is why what happens in it compounds and what happens at four in the afternoon rarely does.
BLOCK What this planner actually does
ITEM Fixes a wake time and tracks whether you held it
ITEM Puts the sequence on paper so the morning is not renegotiated daily
ITEM Separates the body work from the mind work, because they fail differently
ITEM Tracks energy against sleep, so you can see what the routine is buying you
ITEM Gives you a short version for bad mornings, written in advance
BLOCK The honest warning
TEXT A five-step routine held for a year beats a twelve-step routine held for nine days. The Routine Consistency Tracker will show you which one you are running within a fortnight, and it is usually the second.
BLOCK Start small
TEXT Pick three items. Hold them for two weeks. Add nothing until the consistency tracker shows fourteen unbroken days.

PAGE licence
LAYOUT prose
TITLE Licence
SUBTITLE What you may and may not do
BLOCK You may
ITEM Use this planner for your own mornings
ITEM Print unlimited copies for your own use
ITEM Annotate digitally on any device you own
BLOCK You may not
ITEM Resell, share or redistribute the files in any form
ITEM Sell printed copies or distribute copies to clients
ITEM Include the files in another product or bundle
ITEM Claim the design as your own
BLOCK Fonts
